methods.explanation:
A negative exponent of \(-1\) means reciprocal. Since \(a=\tfrac12\ne0\), we have \(a^{-1}=1/a=2\). Substitute this value, evaluating the numerator before dividing by \(a\):
\[
\frac{2a^{-1}+\frac{a^{-1}}2}{a}
=\frac{2\cdot2+\frac22}{\frac12}
=\frac5{\frac12}
=\boxed{10}.
\]
The answer is choice \(\mathrm{D}\).
